@baseUrl=http://localhost:6969
@userId=uuid

### Budget API Testing

### Notes
### ============================================
# How to use this file:
# 1. Set @userId at the top of this file with your user ID
# 2. Run any request - the X-User-ID header will be automatically set
#
# Auth: All requests require the X-User-ID header (set by coregateway)
#
# Endpoints implemented:
# - Expense Categories: full CRUD (soft delete via is_active)
# - Income Categories: full CRUD (soft delete via is_active)
# - Tags: full CRUD (hard delete) + tag associations for expenses/incomes
# - Expenses: full CRUD + search + skip + check-skipped + tag management
# - Incomes: full CRUD + skip + check-skipped + occurrences + tag management
# - Priority Groups: hardcoded reference data (need/want/savings)
# - Budget Remaining: current month income - expenses
# - Stats: summary, trends, category-breakdown, savings-rate
# - Analysis: 50/30/20 breakdown by priority
# - Velocity: average monthly spending
# - Forecast: upcoming recurring expenses
# - Current Total Money: total income - total expenses
# - Month-over-Month: combined monthly trends
# - Recurring Expenses: full CRUD
# - Recurring Incomes: full CRUD
# - Export/Import: JSON backup with ID remapping
# - Health: pgxpool ping + connection stats


### Health Check

GET {{baseUrl}}/health HTTP/1.1

### Expense Categories


### ============================================


### Create Expense Category

POST {{baseUrl}}/budget/expense-categories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-ID: {{userId}}

{
  "name": "Food & Dining",
  "color": "#FF5733",
  "icon": "utensils"
}


### List Expense Categories

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/budget/expense-categories HTTP/1.1
X-User-ID: {{userId}}


### Update Expense Category

PUT {{baseUrl}}/budget/expense-categories/{category_id} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-ID: {{userId}}

{
  "name": "Food & Dining (Updated)",
  "color": "#FF0000",
  "icon": "utensils"
}


### Delete Expense Category

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/budget/expense-categories/{category_id} HTTP/1.1
X-User-ID: {{userId}}


